  "body": "**Description:**\r\n\r\nPlease note, this is Matrix specification extend proposal.\r\nReferring to: https://spec.matrix.org/v1.5/client-server-api/#mtext\r\n\r\nReplies block (see the image below) currently appear only if someone reply a message.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot from 2023-01-02 18-57-47](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/94213268/210222501-553ae99f-a369-4724-8b21-7dbd0b8a85e8.png)\r\n\r\nDrawback of the current way is, users are not aware the message can be replied in a thread without clutter.\r\n\r\nI propose a message-level replies block control property, hypothetically named replyBlock, where message sender control the initial rendering of a message.\r\n\r\nThe replyBlock by default is false as now.\r\n\r\nIf replyBlock is true for the message, then client should render the reply block even for zero reply.\r\n\r\n",
